  website: https://github.com/poplolioi11
abstract: Fu ying xin shuo (婦嬰新說), written by Benjamin Hobson with Guan mao cai and published by Ren ji yi guan in Shanghai in 1858, is a Chinese medical work concerning the female body, pregnancy, childbirth and childhood illnesses, accompanied by medical illustrations. It offers material for the study of nineteenth-century medicine, medical translation and visual culture. Based on Bodleian Libraries, University of Oxford, Sinica 1792, this dataset supplies 137 source faces in JSON, TXT and TEI, preserving source characters, punctuation and uncertainties, with page-level source links and a separately labelled reading file showing note insertions. The transcription is AI-assisted; the nine newly added faces remain initial transcription and have not received expert review.
